  message: "From WI-silos (branch jgstern-agent/fix/silos, commit 41fd9834a6, not yet merged): tuple names, `case let` payloads (switch, if/guard case) and `catch` names are now RECORDED as untyped declarations that shadow (`_declare` in swift.py's binding pass, names from `_swift_pattern_names`). Typing them is now a matter of passing a type at those `_declare` sites instead of None. NOT done by WI-silos: the implicit accessor names `newValue` / `oldValue` and a bare `catch`'s `error` are still not declared at all, so they still fall through to a same-named outer binding or field."  # e223
